 },
 "_swfapi_fluidRender_basis": "1.21.11 fluid rendering API (fabric-rendering-fluids-v1, FluidVariant rendering, BlockRenderLayerMap fluid half): 26.1 Fabric API renders a fluid from a FluidModel per fluid and kept the name FluidRenderHandler for a different interface. The 1.21.11 handler, registry, FluidRendering, DefaultRenderer and SimpleFluidRenderHandler are compat classes with 1.21.11's surface and bodies; rt/CbFapiFluids puts 1.21.11 handlers into 26.1 rendering: FluidStateModelSet.get answers the handler's model (sprites, colour, 1.21.11 layer), FluidRenderer.tesselate of a handled fluid calls renderFluid with the layer's consumer, ModelManager.apply reloads handler textures from the block atlas. FluidVariantRenderHandler.getSprites (dropped) reaches the receiver's override or 1.21.11's default; getColor takes 26.1's client getter.",
 "_swfapi_blockStateModel_basis": "1.21.11 FabricBlockStateModel / WrapperBlockStateModel / FabricBlockModels: 26.1 takes the client BlockAndTintGetter in emitQuads, createGeometryKey and the particle lookups (callReshapes, super calls included, plus override hooks), renamed particleSprite / getModelParticleSprite to particleMaterial / getParticleMaterial (Material.Baked; calls read its sprite, overrides answer a material without forced translucency), and WrapperBlockStateModel no longer forwards the vanilla collectParts(random) / particleIcon() 26.1 removed (calls take CbWallModels' 1.21.11 bodies on the receiver, super calls the wrapped model's). The facade BlockModelShaper (1.21.11 class_773, into which FabricBlockModels was injected) implements 26.1 FabricBlockStateModelSet from its own models.",
 "_swfapi_renderer_basis": "1.21.11 Fabric renderer entry points: 26.1 removed Renderer.render x2 / renderBlockAsEntity / getLayerRenderStateEmitter, FabricBlockModelRenderer, FabricBlockRenderManager, BlockVertexConsumerProvider and RenderLayerHelper (blocks tesselate through AltModelBlockRenderer into a QuadEmitter). The interfaces and helper are compat classes with 1.21.11's surface; rt/CbFapiRender runs Indigo's terrain-like path on 26.1's AltModelBlockRenderer and its simple path on the model's emitQuads (tint, emissive / maxLight, QuadView.buffer per chunk layer). A call through ModelBlockRenderer (26.1's does not implement the interface) reaches a mod subclass's override or 1.21.11's default; the BlockRenderDispatcher facade implements FabricBlockRenderManager. As 1.21.11's Fabric API overwrote them, renderBreakingTexture / renderSingleBlock (facade) and ModelBlockRenderer.renderModel (CbWallBlockRender) go through the same paths. The item layer render type getter (Renderer.setLayerRenderTypeGetter, FabricLayerRenderState.setRenderTypeGetter; ItemRenderTypeGetter compat) is kept on the layer and applied to the layer mesh's quads at its submit (rt/CbFapiLayerRenderTypes), where 1.21.11 asked it per quad at render time."
}
